Subject: winex11: advertise the minimize and maximize Motif functions for disabled windows

Patch 0037 moved MWM_FUNC_CLOSE out of the WS_DISABLED gate. The
minimize and maximize functions still vanish while a window is
disabled, and WMs derive _NET_WM_ALLOWED_ACTIONS from the Motif
functions, so hints computed while a startup modal holds the main
window disabled make mutter refuse even the application's own
programmatic SW_SHOWMAXIMIZED restore. An application that replays a
saved maximized placement while its startup modal is up stays at the
restored size instead: the measured trace shows functions 0x26 against
decorations 0x7a.

Windows keeps both buttons visible on a disabled window and refuses
the interaction at the input layer. Advertise the functions
unconditionally, for the same reason as the close function.

diff --git a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
index 9208df5..c19a0ec 100644
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
@@ -1152,18 +1152,23 @@ static void set_mwm_hints( struct x11drv_win_data *data, UINT style, UINT ex_sty
          * disabled, so the visible button is a no-op, same as on Windows. */
         mwm_hints.functions = MWM_FUNC_MOVE | MWM_FUNC_CLOSE;
         if (is_window_resizable( data, style )) mwm_hints.functions |= MWM_FUNC_RESIZE;
-        if (!(style & WS_DISABLED))
-        {
-            if (style & WS_MINIMIZEBOX) mwm_hints.functions |= MWM_FUNC_MINIMIZE;
-            if (style & WS_MAXIMIZEBOX) mwm_hints.functions |= MWM_FUNC_MAXIMIZE;
-
-            /* The window can be programmatically minimized even without
-               a minimize box button. Allow the WM to restore it. */
-            if (style & WS_MINIMIZE)    mwm_hints.functions |= MWM_FUNC_MINIMIZE | MWM_FUNC_MAXIMIZE;
-            /* The window can be programmatically maximized even without
-               a maximize box button. Allow the WM to maximize it. */
-            if (style & WS_MAXIMIZE)    mwm_hints.functions |= MWM_FUNC_MAXIMIZE;
-        }
+        /* Like MWM_FUNC_CLOSE above, the minimize and maximize functions must
+         * not depend on WS_DISABLED.  WMs derive _NET_WM_ALLOWED_ACTIONS from
+         * these hints, so hints computed while a startup modal holds the window
+         * disabled make mutter refuse even the application's own programmatic
+         * SW_SHOWMAXIMIZED restore (Lightroom Classic replays its saved
+         * maximized placement behind the modal and stays at the restored size).
+         * Windows keeps the buttons visible on a disabled window and refuses
+         * the interaction at the input layer instead. */
+        if (style & WS_MINIMIZEBOX) mwm_hints.functions |= MWM_FUNC_MINIMIZE;
+        if (style & WS_MAXIMIZEBOX) mwm_hints.functions |= MWM_FUNC_MAXIMIZE;
+
+        /* The window can be programmatically minimized even without
+           a minimize box button. Allow the WM to restore it. */
+        if (style & WS_MINIMIZE)    mwm_hints.functions |= MWM_FUNC_MINIMIZE | MWM_FUNC_MAXIMIZE;
+        /* The window can be programmatically maximized even without
+           a maximize box button. Allow the WM to maximize it. */
+        if (style & WS_MAXIMIZE)    mwm_hints.functions |= MWM_FUNC_MAXIMIZE;
     }
 
     mwm_hints.flags = MWM_HINTS_FUNCTIONS | MWM_HINTS_DECORATIONS;
